== points to gp ratio ==

For the rewards, it looks like (at least early on) that the gp per reward is roughly 8*points.



So for 30,000 points it looks like the rewards will be each 240k (roughly). Hopefully this stays true, but in order to prove it there needs to be lots of documented cases of high scoring games to get the error as small as possible.



For example, right now 1 rune ore can be obtained with 214 points or with 2400, with high scoring games the numbers will get more precise.
